gcontent-ng-c373336239="" _nghost-ng-c373336239=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-ng-c373336239="" class="ng-star-inserted">Build a complete production-ready Android app called "PDF Maker Studio" using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose (Material 3).Core Features:1. Authentication:   - Email + Password registration and login   - Google Sign-In (complete working implementation with Activity Result API)   - Proper logout   - Show logged-in user's email in the top bar2. PDF Creation:   - Create PDF from multiple images (user can select multiple images at once)   - Create PDF from text (user can enter title + body text)   - Support Bengali text properly in PDF (use a good Bengali font if possible, or handle Unicode correctly)   - Generated PDFs should be A4 size3. Cloud Features (Firebase):   - Upload generated PDFs to Firebase Cloud Storage under users/{uid}/pdfs/   - Save PDF metadata (name, url, storagePath, createdAt) in Firestore under users/{uid}/pdfs/   - Show "My Cloud Files" list with:     - Open PDF     - Rename PDF     - Delete PDF (delete from both Storage and Firestore)   - Real-time or pull-to-refresh file list   - Only the logged-in user can see and manage their own files4. UI/UX:   - Modern, clean Material 3 design   - Beautiful gradient header   - Smooth loading states and progress indicators   - Clear success/error messages (Snackbar)   - Fully support Bengali UI text where appropriate   - Responsive and nice looking cards for actions and file list5. Extra Requirements:   - Proper Firebase Security Rules for Firestore and Storage (user can only access their own data)   - Handle loading, error, and empty states properly   - Use latest stable libraries and best practices   - Clean architecture (don't put everything in one Activity if possible)   - Package name: com.pdfmakerstudio.appPlease set up Firebase automatically (Authentication with Email/Password + Google, Firestore, and Cloud Storage) and generate 